From: hazeldo <haze@lxcamail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:03:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Do not trust install and backup paths from
 app_location.json blindly

app_location.json lives in %APPDATA% and can be rewritten by any program
running as the user. Its currentAppPath was wiped and refilled by
'MagicChatbox.exe -update', '-rollback' and the restore paths, and its
backupPath was deleted by '-clearbackup' and copied into the install by
'-rollback'. When the copy failed with access denied, the updater raised
its own UAC prompt and repeated the operation elevated, so a user-level
attacker could have MagicChatbox wipe a protected folder, fill it with
files from the user-writable update workspace and start them as admin.

The install directory must now contain MagicChatbox.exe and must not be
a drive root, the Windows directory or a personal/system folder, and the
backup must live inside MagicChatbox's own data folder. This also stops
an update from wiping Downloads or Desktop for users who unpacked the
app directly into one of those folders.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
